{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX of 0xa5 never completes on ser_tx so recv never gets a byte vs expected 0xa5, ending in TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received. send_bitcnt at line 132 decrements by 2 per bit-time so the 10-bit frame {1'b1,data,1'b0} shifts only 5 times and truncates. CONE_SLICE has no simpleuart coverage so trace wins and line 132 is the root cause.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -130,5 +130,5 @@
 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
-				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 2;
+				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, loopback byte 0xa5 received with no uart timeout"}

